Fix the non-Fortran fallback in grace_np/gracef_np.c.

When configure is run with --enable-f77-wrapper=no, config.h never defines
F77_FNAME, so the "keep the translation unit non-empty" dummy expands to the
malformed declarator `void F77_FNAME(_gracef_np_c_dummy_func)(void){}`. clang
16+ rejects this as "function cannot return function type 'void (void)'" and
the grace_np subdir fails to build. The dummy does not need name mangling; drop
F77_FNAME so the fallback compiles regardless of the wrapper setting.

--- a/grace_np/gracef_np.c
+++ b/grace_np/gracef_np.c
@@ -78,6 +78,6 @@
 #else /* don't include Fortran wrapper */

 /* To make ANSI C happy about non-empty file */
-void F77_FNAME(_gracef_np_c_dummy_func) (void) {}
+void _gracef_np_c_dummy_func (void) {}

 #endif /* WITH_F77_WRAPPER */
